From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:29:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 36/75] PlaitOS: slide on the status bar to change brightness

Port of crDroid's status bar brightness control as it stands after its
fixes (crDroid frameworks_base 16.0):
  08a17c17e SystemUI: Port statusbar brightness control (Alberto97; a squash
            of the CyanogenMod/LineageOS changes by Danesh Mondegarian, Roman
            Birg, Pawit Pornkitprasan, Zhao Wei Liew, Chenyang Zhong,
            jhenrique09 and cjh1249131356)
  22090b794 SystemUI: Fix and add status bar brightness control for lockscreen
  d1ea8e093 SystemUI: Fix quick pulldown regression (already the order in
            GrapheneOS, nothing to port)
  49509c18c SystemUI: Fix sporadic jumps in statusbar brightness control
            (all three by Pranav Vashi)

Applied by hand: crDroid's CentralSurfacesImpl differs too much from
GrapheneOS's for the patches to place reliably.

PlaitOS changes:
- Switches are Settings.System plait_status_bar_brightness_control and
  plait_status_bar_brightness_control_lockscreen (both off by default),
  read once per touch-down for the current user (GrapheneOS's shade has no
  tuner hook)
- A slide starts from the screen's real brightness instead of the value the
  last slide left behind, which made the first slide after boot or after the
  Quick Settings slider jump
- No settings write on every move: like the Quick Settings slider, the
  brightness is temporary while dragging and saved once by setBrightness()
  when the finger lifts
- CentralSurfaces gets default no-op methods, so other implementations are
  untouched

